WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.471
Andhra Pradesh's monsoon has a distant connection: the Pacific Ocean.

00:00:05.471 --> 00:00:13.595
Normally, trade winds push warm surface water towards Indonesia. Cold water rises near South America.

00:00:13.595 --> 00:00:20.170
During El Nino, trade winds weaken. Warmth spreads east and tropical rainfall shifts.

00:00:20.170 --> 00:00:24.865
Major events include nineteen ninety seven and twenty fifteen.

00:00:24.865 --> 00:00:44.142
NOAA's July to September ocean index is plus 2.16 degrees. Its October eighth outlook projects a relative-index peak of 2.74 degrees. Strong to very strong conditions remain over eighty three percent likely through March. This is not an Andhra Pradesh rainfall forecast.

00:00:44.142 --> 00:00:50.142
India's summer monsoon can weaken. The Indian Ocean and local weather also matter.

00:00:50.142 --> 00:00:58.142
5 of 7 El Nino summer monsoons were below average in Andhra Pradesh, averaging 13 percent below.

00:00:58.142 --> 00:01:07.783
June to August 2026 rainfall was 41.5 percent below average. Rank 1 driest in 46 years.

00:01:07.783 --> 00:01:20.265
Historically, El Nino northeast monsoons averaged 7.7 percent below normal: 9 of 15 years. The north coast fared worst. This season has only just begun.

00:01:20.265 --> 00:01:26.434
Rain infiltrates soil and fractured rock. Pumping and geology shape what remains.

00:01:26.434 --> 00:01:36.434
By September, 54.3 percent of compared mandals were deeper than in May. 85.7 percent were short of their own ten year normal.

00:01:36.434 --> 00:01:42.731
District shortfalls differ. These are medians of observations, not predictions.

00:01:42.731 --> 00:01:54.482
The State's 1746 station network reads 11.43 metres below ground on September ninth, 3.18 metres deeper than a year earlier.

00:01:54.482 --> 00:02:05.505
Orvakal reads 29.68 metres. Water is 14.61 metres deeper this season, instead of its usual 2.36 metre rise.

00:02:05.505 --> 00:02:10.505
Less recharge and continued pumping can increase pressure on wells.

00:02:10.505 --> 00:02:27.666
Past winters project 126 mandals beyond their deepest May. 76 are already over ten metres deep, home to about sixty seven lakh people in twenty twenty. Historically, only 32.5 percent of beyond-record calls materialised.

00:02:27.666 --> 00:02:40.581
As of October tenth, 477 mandals meet the rainfall trigger. 30 read severe, 325 moderate. This is manual evidence, not a drought declaration.

00:02:40.581 --> 00:02:50.861
For a possible dry spell: protect drinking water. Use drip irrigation and mulch where suitable. Agree a village contingency plan with local teams.

00:02:50.861 --> 00:03:01.045
Cities cannot stop El Nino. Repair mains. Reuse safely treated water for non-drinking needs. Protect lakes and essential supplies.

00:03:01.045 --> 00:03:12.950
Read observations, NOAA's Pacific forecast, and the summer projection separately. None forecasts Andhra Pradesh rainfall. Verify locally. Assign action.
